{
  "key": "gh-1061",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "Blocked-rework comment: thread dump drowns response.md, and null-id machine notices make the gh-957 coverage gate unsatisfiable (live: dart gh-395 week-long loop)",
    "description": "## Goal — blocked-rework comment delivers the agent's message, not a thread dump (v1)\n\nOne sentence: **the blocked-rework PR comment becomes the agent's response.md** — the thread-coverage evidence moves to a folded appendix.\n\nToday `handleReworkBlocked` (js/pushReworkChanges.js) composes one PR comment that leads with every unaddressed review thread inline-quoted (`no-id — \"<100 chars>\"` × N) and appends the agent's `outputs/response.md` only when present. On the very passes where the agent most needs a human (blocked, needs a decision), the actionable text is buried under the dump — or absent entirely when the leg failed to write the file. Live evidence: dmtools-dart gh-395 / PR #420, 2026-10-18, run 39156398849 — 39 threads dumped, the leg's API-choice question visible only in the raw run log; the same PR has been blocked-looping for a week because 16 open threads are machine notices with `null threadId` that can never receive a targeted reply.\n\n## Why this framing\n\n- The prompt contract already mandates `outputs/response.md` on blocked passes (agents/instructions/pr_rework/output_rules.md:46, pr_rework_prompt.md:127 \"SHORT general PR comment\"). The defect is in the **post-action composition and the gate arithmetic**, not in agent compliance — so the fix lands in the pack code, with the prompt strengthened only where the contract is ambiguous (see AC5).\n\n## Root causes (one code path, two defects)\n\n1. **Inline enumeration.** The gh-957 coverage-gate sentence maps every unaddressed thread through `threadLabel()` into the comment body before the agent's text.\n2. **Unsatisfiable denominator.** Threads with `null threadId` (machine notices: red-head markers, `rework-consume` payloads, prior blocked comments) cannot receive targeted replies — `outputs/review_replies.json` addresses threads by id. A PR whose open threads are all null-id can never pass the coverage gate → guaranteed infinite blocked loop.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (testable)\n\n- **AC1** — The blocked comment leads with the agent's `outputs/response.md` content verbatim (subject: the comment body; first visible block after the ⚠️ header line).\n- **AC2** — The unaddressed-thread enumeration renders inside a collapsed `<details>` block, capped at 3 inline previews + \"…and N more\", full list inside the fold. Comment body stays under ~2000 chars for a 39-thread case.\n- **AC3** — Threads with `null` threadId are excluded from the coverage-gate denominator (they are counted and reported as informational context in the fold). A PR whose only open threads are null-id notices does NOT enter the blocked path on coverage grounds.\n- **AC4** — When the leg wrote no `outputs/response.md` on a blocked pass, the comment says so explicitly (\"agent wrote no response.md — see run log <url>\") instead of silently omitting the agent's side.\n- **AC5** — The rework prompt's blocked contract gains one sentence: \"Even when blocked or awaiting a human decision, ALWAYS write outputs/response.md — it is posted as the PR comment; nothing in the run log reaches the human otherwise.\"\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `UT-1` — 39-thread blocked case: comment < 2000 chars, response.md first, fold present (AC1/AC2). Maps to existing `test_pushReworkChanges.js` suites.\n- `UT-2` — all-open-threads-null-id: blocked path NOT taken on coverage grounds (AC3).\n- `UT-3` — missing response.md on blocked pass: explicit placeholder sentence (AC4).\n- `UT-4` — mixed null-id + addressable threads: denominator counts only addressable ones (AC3).\n- `REG-1` — existing gh-957 coverage-gate tests (addressable unaddressed threads still block) stay green unchanged.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing gh-957 gate semantics for addressable threads (targeted replies stay mandatory).\n- Resolving null-id threads automatically or assigning them synthetic ids.\n- Touching the non-blocked completion comment path (`postCompletionPrComment`) beyond keeping it consistent.\n\n## References\n\n- js/pushReworkChanges.js `handleReworkBlocked`, `evaluateAuditResolveGate`\n- agents/prompts/pr_rework_prompt.md:127, agents/instructions/pr_rework/output_rules.md:46\n- Live incident: dmtools-dart PR #420 / gh-395, run 39156398849 (2026-10-18)\n\n## Machine jobs\n- [x] ▶ dev (fa-bug-dev) · [run](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/39158688330) · started 19:25 · done 19:38 ✅"
  }
}===DIFF===
# PR Diff Truncated

