{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `totalOpenCount` is returned but never consumed**

`buildReplyCoverage` now returns `totalOpenCount: open.length`, but no production caller reads it — the only reference is the new unit test asserting its value. Either wire it in (e.g. the blocked-comment fold could report "N open in total, M addressable" so the header count and the fold stay reconcilable) or drop the field to keep the coverage contract minimal. As-is it is dead API surface that future readers must assume is load-bearing.
