{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `totalOpenCount` is returned but never consumed**

`buildReplyCoverage` now returns `totalOpenCount: open.length`, but no production caller reads it — the only reference is the new unit test asserting its value. Either wire it in (e.g. the blocked-comment fold could report "N open in total, M addressable" so the header count and the fold stay reconcilable) or drop the field to keep the coverage contract minimal. As-is it is dead API surface that future readers must assume is load-bearing.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `isUnaddressableThread` is evaluated twice per open thread**

`buildReplyCoverage` computes the unaddressable set with one `filter(isUnaddressableThread)` pass and then the addressable set with a second, negated `filter`. `threadKeyOf()` is cheap so this is not a performance issue, but the two filters are one classification viewed twice — a single pass building both buckets (or deriving `addressable = open` minus the unaddressable set) would be clearer and cannot drift if the predicate ever becomes more expensive. Minor; fold into the CRAP-split cleanup if you touch this function anyway.
